      "message": "nit. I think we might be able to special case this in the generator such that any server-side commands that return a `WGPUStatus`, should check that it\u0027s success, otherwise it is probably a fatal error. For the most part, I think that all such commands are currently implemented on the client side, but given that commands that return a `WGPUStatus` are all synchronous, it probably makes sense to default to making the server doers do the check unconditionally if they aren\u0027t being manually implemented on the client side.\n\nI think that would mean we wouldn\u0027t need to introduce new commands in dawn_wire.json for these, and that they wouldn\u0027t need to be under `client_side_commands`. I think that `ResourceTableInsertBinding` would still need to be under there though since we manually implement that to use `Update` instead.",
